A||||3||gtsonly||Engine Good-Shifting Bad.... Help Please, Please!!!||||5||
Z||000000||gtsonly||12-26-2001||02:48 PM||||Before the engine build I noticed if the car was cold I could only shift into 1st and 2nd, after a few minutes she would shift normal. I just finished the engine build and got into the car without it even started and went to shift threw the gears. I can only shift 1st and 2nd, if I try to shift to 3rd it feels like it is binding up and it wont allow me to move the shifter to the right at all. Whats going on!!!!!!????????<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-26-2001||02:58 PM||||Sounds like the problem I had..<P>I changed the transmission fluid to "GM Syncromesh" and have no further problems..<P>However, I've seen a lot of posts with this problem. Some were different fixes. Might check the "search" area and get more advice.<P>Might have a binding cable somewhere.<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">     <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hairy_Fiero||12-26-2001||03:12 PM||||Sounds like your "selector cable". This is what controls the right to left movement of your shifter which is the narrow diameter cable connected to your gear shifter. The larger diameter cable is the shift cable, and this cable controls the forward to back motion of the gear shift. Sounds like you need to atleast replace the selector cable. If the forward to back motion is "tough" then it may also be a good idea to replace the the shift cable while you tackle the selector. Good luck!<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000003||Elvira||12-28-2001||07:59 AM||||I had the exact same problem in my 86GT 5 speed.  My should hurt after driving up the road and back it was so hard to shift.  5th and reverse were not happening!  I changed the selector cable and she shifts great now!  It was really easy to change.  Thook me about a half hour from start to finish.<P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles<BR>84 Indy<BR>87 4-seater||||reg||1
